data_mmcif_ma-annotation.dic
# Proposed component; no released dictionary is superseded.
_pdbx_dictionary_component.datablock_id mmcif_ma-annotation.dic
_pdbx_dictionary_component.dictionary_component_id mmcif_ma-annotation.dic
_pdbx_dictionary_component.title 'ModelCIF annotation storage compatible with AtomWorks'
_pdbx_dictionary_component.version 0.3.0
_pdbx_dictionary_component_history.dictionary_component_id mmcif_ma-annotation.dic
_pdbx_dictionary_component_history.version 0.3.0
_pdbx_dictionary_component_history.update 2026-11-15
_pdbx_dictionary_component_history.revision 'Define existing annotation columns and idx/val tables with ModelCIF context.'

save_ma_annotation_context
_category.description
;
Data items in this category identify one annotation snapshot in the data block and its ModelCIF data artifact. A block has one authored, effective or derived snapshot. Separate snapshots use separate blocks/files, linked by existing ModelCIF data groups and protocol steps. Model-specific payloads refer to ma_model_list through model_num; a model-free zero-body extension can use entry scope.
;
_category.id ma_annotation_context
_category.mandatory_code no
loop_
_category_key.name
'_ma_annotation_context.entry_id'
loop_
_category_group.id
inclusive_group
ma_group
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.entry_id
_item_description.description
;
Entry containing the annotation snapshot.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.entry_id'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code code
_item_linked.child_name '_ma_annotation_context.entry_id'
_item_linked.parent_name '_entry.id'
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.data_id
_item_description.description
;
Annotation data artifact, distinct from the coordinate artifact. Use ma_data content_type other and describe the annotations.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.data_id'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code int
_item_linked.child_name '_ma_annotation_context.data_id'
_item_linked.parent_name '_ma_data.id'
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.stage
_item_description.description
;
Authored request, effective values consumed by software after preprocessing/default generation, or derived annotation output.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.stage'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code code
loop_
_item_enumeration.value
authored
effective
derived
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.required_for_execution
_item_description.description
;
If True, consumers must understand and resolve every supplied input condition and its referenced profile before execution. Preserving bytes alone is insufficient. This flag does not claim output satisfaction.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.required_for_execution'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code code
loop_
_item_enumeration.value
True
False
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.profile_uri
_item_description.description
;
Resolvable version-specific specification of scientific algorithms, partner contexts, tokenization and other execution choices not fixed by individual dictionary items. Must not redefine dictionary meanings. If required meaning is unavailable, execution fails explicitly.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.profile_uri'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code line
save_

save__ma_annotation_context.details
_item_description.description
;
Additional annotation preparation or interpretation details.
;
_item.name '_ma_annotation_context.details'
_item.category_id ma_annotation_context
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code text
save_

save__atom_site.ma_atom_array_index
_item_description.description
;
Saved zero-based atom-array index, unique within pdbx_PDB_model_num. Annotation idx0/idx1 refer to this value in the same model, never to the current row number. Required for indexed annotations; retain or consistently remap it when rows are reordered, filtered or copied.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_atom_array_index'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_token_id
_item_description.description
;
Token membership label, unique per token within the model; all member atoms carry the same label. Required when token-level annotations or token offsets are exchanged. The preprocessing profile identifies the tokenizer.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_token_id'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code code
save_

save__atom_site.ma_molecule_id
_item_description.description
;
Molecule membership label within the model. Required when molecule-level annotations or molecule-scoped index groups are exchanged. Every token belongs to one molecule.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_molecule_id'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code code
save_

save__atom_site.ma_token_index
_item_description.description
;
Integer token offset shared by all atoms of a token. For index-group conditioning, differences are meaningful only inside the same model, molecule and index group. Origins are arbitrary and offsets unique within that scope.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_token_index'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_annotation_expsegmin_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Minimum realized residue count for an expandable input segment marker; -1 means this residue is not a segment marker. Active bounds must be nonnegative and paired with expsegmax. Marker residues describe algorithmic input positions, not extra experimentally observed residues; their marker status and handling must be retained.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_annotation_expsegmin_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_annotation_expsegmax_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Maximum realized residue count for an expandable input segment marker; -1 means inactive. An active maximum must be at least the corresponding minimum. Zero permits deletion. These input bounds do not assert an output realization.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_annotation_expsegmax_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_atomize
_item_description.description
;
Per-atom request to treat its residue atomistically. True requests atomistic treatment; False requests the declared polymer tokenization. Effective files materialize the resulting token membership and the structure-dependent default. This flag alone does not define a tokenizer.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_atomize'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code code
loop_
_item_enumeration.value
True
False
save_

save__atom_site.ma_condition_sequence_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Requested residue component identity, broadcast over all atoms of the residue. <M> means no identity request; a different string must identify a chem_comp record. The reference residue identity is not itself a condition. Explicit component probabilities must agree with an exact identity.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_condition_sequence_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code line
save_

save_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_category.description
;
Absolute Cartesian coordinate target in angstroms in the coordinate frame of the selected model. val0, val1 and val2 are x, y and z. A target is a complete finite triple; three inapplicable values mean no target. Partial triples and infinities are invalid. These are values, not a mask over atom_site coordinates. Body order 1; semantic level atom. Indices identify atoms; broadcasts retain the stated level. Composite model/index reference rules are defined in the accompanying contract.
;
_category.id ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_category.mandatory_code no
loop_
_category_key.name
'_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.model_num'
'_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.idx0'
loop_
_category_group.id
inclusive_group
ma_group
save_

save__ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.model_num
_item_description.description
;
Model containing all indexed atoms in this row. Required even for a single model.
;
_item.name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.model_num'
_item.category_id ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code int
_item_linked.child_name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.model_num'
_item_linked.parent_name '_ma_model_list.ordinal_id'
save_

save__ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.idx0
_item_description.description
;
Saved atom-array index of operand 0. Resolve jointly with model_num to atom_site.ma_atom_array_index and pdbx_PDB_model_num.
;
_item.name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.idx0'
_item.category_id ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_item.mandatory_code yes
_item_type.code int
_item_linked.child_name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.idx0'
_item_linked.parent_name '_atom_site.ma_atom_array_index'
save_

save__ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.val0
_item_description.description
;
Absolute Cartesian coordinate target in angstroms in the coordinate frame of the selected model. val0, val1 and val2 are x, y and z. A target is a complete finite triple; three inapplicable values mean no target. Partial triples and infinities are invalid. These are values, not a mask over atom_site coordinates. This item is the x component.
;
_item.name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.val0'
_item.category_id ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code float
_item_units.code angstroms
save_

save__ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.val1
_item_description.description
;
Absolute Cartesian coordinate target in angstroms in the coordinate frame of the selected model. val0, val1 and val2 are x, y and z. A target is a complete finite triple; three inapplicable values mean no target. Partial triples and infinities are invalid. These are values, not a mask over atom_site coordinates. This item is the y component.
;
_item.name '_ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.val1'
_item.category_id ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code float
_item_units.code angstroms
save_

save__ma_condition_coordinate_1_atom.val2
_item_description.description
;
Absolute Cartesian coordinate target in angstroms in the coordinate frame of the selected model. val0, val1 and val2 are x, y and z. A target is a complete finite triple; three inapplicable values mean no target. Partial triples and infinities are invalid. These are values, not a mask over atom_site coordinates. This item is the z component.
