save__atom_site.ma_condition_secondary_structure_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Residue-level secondary-structure code: 0 inactive, 1 helix (DSSP H/G/I), 2 sheet (E/B), 3 loop (T/S/C/P), 4 non-protein or assignment failure. Code 4 preserves the source distinction from an ordinary loop but does not distinguish non-protein from assignment failure. The profile must identify assignment method/version and handling of code 4.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_condition_secondary_structure_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
loop_
_item_enumeration.value
0
1
2
3
4
save_

save__atom_site.ma_condition_index_group_1_token
_item_description.description
;
Integer equivalence class of known token-index offsets, broadcast per token. The key is (model, molecule, group), not the integer alone. Effective files supply token membership and token_index; differences inside a group are meaningful, differences between groups are unspecified. Group labels may be renamed consistently.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_condition_index_group_1_token'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_condition_cath_label_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Requested CATH classification label, broadcast per residue. x.x.x.x is inactive. The execution profile must specify the CATH release, hierarchy level and how residue labels map to domains.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_condition_cath_label_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code line
save_

save_ma_condition_InternalCoordinate_1_atom
_category.description
;
Cartesian XYZ targets in angstroms local to a positive CoordinateGroup. These are not bond-angle or torsion coordinates. A group may rotate and translate as a whole. Every member of a positive group must have a complete finite triple; members outside positive groups have no internal target. Body order 1; semantic level atom. Indices identify atoms; broadcasts retain the stated level. Composite model/index reference rules are defined in the accompanying contract.
;
_category.id ma_condition_InternalCoordinate_1_atom
_category.mandatory_code no
