save__atom_site.ma_annotation_src_coordinate_conditioned_region_1_atom
_item_description.description
;
Local source label for the coordinate-conditioned region. A literal quoted period is the source inactive sentinel; it is distinct from a CIF null. A short label is not a global atom or artifact identity. Exact correspondence requires a declared source mapping in the execution profile and ModelCIF data/file provenance.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_annotation_src_coordinate_conditioned_region_1_atom'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code line
save_

save__atom_site.ma_annotation_src_component_1_atom
_item_description.description
;
Local label for the source component. A literal quoted period means unassigned and is distinct from a CIF null. It does not identify a chem_comp chemical component or a globally unique source artifact. Resolve provenance through declared data/file records and a source mapping.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_annotation_src_component_1_atom'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code line
save_

save__atom_site.ma_annotation_src_index_group_1_atom
_item_description.description
;
Original index-group label for an unindexed insertion; -1 means not mapped. Its source context must be recorded before it can identify an external group. Preserve the numeric payload without inferring correspondence from the number alone.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_annotation_src_index_group_1_atom'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code int
save_

save__atom_site.ma_is_unindexed_insertion
_item_description.description
;
Per-atom derived flag identifying an output location mapped from an unindexed in-context input token. True marks an insertion target and False does not. Full input/output correspondence needs source identity and producing protocol provenance.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_is_unindexed_insertion'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code code
loop_
_item_enumeration.value
True
False
save_

save_ma_annotation_coords_with_insertion_1_atom
_category.description
;
Derived reference XYZ in angstroms: absolute targets plus group-local targets superposed into the generated model frame. Missing targets are inapplicable. This is saved reference geometry, not a quality score; record the producing protocol and use existing ModelCIF QA categories for evaluated RMSD. Body order 1; semantic level atom. Indices identify atoms; broadcasts retain the stated level. Composite model/index reference rules are defined in the accompanying contract.
;
