save__atom_site.ma_condition_sequence_probability_ALA_1_residue
_item_description.description
;
Explicit probability for component ALA, broadcast per residue. Finite values lie in [0,1]; zero excludes this component. A period means no supplied probability; a question mark means unknown and cannot be silently executed. Supplied probabilities sum to at most one; a complete distribution sums to one (tolerance 1e-6). Unspecified candidates may share remaining mass without implicit renormalization. Exact identity, if supplied, fixes a consistent one-hot distribution. The candidate identity is ALA, not a private channel index. Referenced chemical components require chem_comp definitions.
;
_item.name '_atom_site.ma_condition_sequence_probability_ALA_1_residue'
_item.category_id atom_site
_item.mandatory_code no
_item_type.code float
save_

